    <h2>What I Loved</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>A crazy and distinctive visual style that commits completely to its own weirdness.</li>
        <li>Chaotic boulder levels that are easy to understand but difficult to truly master.</li>
        <li>Challenging Tower Defence-style levels that require a completely different kind of thinking.</li>
        <li>Hilarious use of animated historical portraits throughout the presentation.</li>
        <li>An epic soundtrack featuring some brilliant rock remixes of classical music.</li>
        <li>A wonderfully goofy sense of humour that was completely to my taste.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What Didn't Work</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>The gameplay could become repetitive during longer stretches of play.</li>
        <li>Progress became more difficult once I had completed the levels that played to my strengths.</li>
        <li>The very goofy humour could become grating for players who do not connect with its particular style.</li>
    </ul>

